<title>BELGIUM: EU clears AXA acquisition of UAP.</title>
<headline>EU clears AXA acquisition of UAP.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it had cleared an operation under which French insurance company AXA will acquire sole control of rival company Union des Assurances de Paris (UAP) in a share swap.  </p>
<p>The Commission said the new group, AXA/UAP, would be active in the markets for life and non-life insurance, reinsurance and financial services. It would become leading European insurer in terms of premium income.</p>
<p>&quot;The Commission considers that the operation could create risks of a dominant position emerging but indicates that it has taken into account the capacity for customer demand to stimulate competition...as well as the presence of other competitors on the market,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>It cited other major players such as Germany's Allianz and Italy's Generali. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
